  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Capacity building for INMG Improving meteorological services Cabo Verde</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Netherlands finances private sector development projects in Cabo Verde in the tourism and maritime industries.For the development of those sectors, improved seasonal forecasts are of importance, for example predicting droughts, hurricanes and dust storms and in the long term sea level and sea temperature rise.KNMI assists the Cabo Verde Meteorological Institute INMG with the organization of a climate database and advices INMG on climate modeling, scenarios and forecasts.INMG staff capacity is built to improve weather forecasting and economic relevant climate information for the end users in agriculture, tourism, marine services and aviation. INMG is also assisted in the process of joining relevant and useful international cooperation programmes like Green Climate Fund, the Global Centre in Adaptation, the coalition of climate vulnerable forum countries and climate risk and early warning systems (CREWS West Africa).</narrative>
  </description>
